{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/693","id":4729537258,"node_id":"PR_kwDORnQJEs8AAAABGecC6g","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/693","diff_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/693.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/693.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/issues/693","number":693,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(push): push delivery, send-time quiet hours, emitter wiring (split P2 of #648)","user":{"login":"BradleyGleavePortfolio","id":264851314,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8lPcg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264851314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tier: T4\nWhy: Sends device pushes to locked screens from a shared outbox with consent, quiet hours and token cleanup; a fault leaks private detail, ignores a mute, or sends to a dead or reassigned device.\nT4 trigger scan: lock-screen copy at send, push tokens (DeviceNotRegistered cleanup), consent at send time, multi-replica claim/lease concurrency, inbox visibility of stored notifications.\nT3 trigger scan: booking lifecycle emitters, drip, purchase and payout notice writers.\nBounded T1: NO.\nCanonical builder: T4 builder lane B-PUSH2-120 (agent 120 wave).\nParent owner: operator (agent 120 wave).\nAcceptance evidence: test/push-delivery-round5.spec.ts (15 cases), Sol P2 probe 7/7, Opus U1/U4 and live L1-L6 on Postgres at 53796f1e (ci-lane run 37352088482); every required PR check green at the exact head; Opus and Sol verdicts at the exact head.\nPromotion triggers: already T4. Any change to the claim SQL, consent checks, token handling or lock-screen copy needs fresh dual exact-head verdicts.\n\n## Fix rounds\n| Round | Head | Finding | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5 (B-PUSH2-120) | c2cef1d1 | main refresh | merged P1 (with main ee55f814); conflict in CreateNotificationInput resolved keeping main's `throttle_key` and P2's `push_twin`; main's channelGate/gateFrom/describeFailure kept |\n| 5 | c2cef1d1 | Opus B-693-1 channelId | per-kind Android channel from the app's own set (coach-messages, client-bot, milestones, system); `default` removed; set pinned by a test |\n| 5 | c2cef1d1 | Sol B-693-1 reschedule dedupe | dedupe identity per move (`booking_rescheduled:<session>:<session updated_at>`); fallback old>new times |\n| 5 | c2cef1d1 | Sol B-648-7 hidden sole rows | `push_twin` hides a push row only when its inapp counterpart (same user, kind, link, text, last hour) is stored; drip and purchase writers pass whether their inapp row was written |\n| 5 | c2cef1d1 | Sol B-693-2 failed token clear | a failed clear is kept as `token-cleanup-pending` and retried by the receipt sweep (clear only, never the push) |\n| 5 | c2cef1d1 | Sol B-648-9 consent during preparation | preferences and token read again after the handoff write; mute, per-kind switch off or sign-out stops the send |\n| 5 | c2cef1d1 | Sol B-692-1 (defense in depth) | worker always renders the kind's template at send; booking push context no longer stores display names |\n| 5 | c2cef1d1 | Opus C-693-2 (operator-approved) | payout notice push row `push_twin: true` |\n| 5 | 53796f1e | main guard test/privacy/no-pii-in-logs.spec.ts | onModuleInit log variable renamed (same text) |\n\n## Split description (written at 13417e7b; counts in it are from that head)\nSplit of #648 (device push delivery with quiet hours; 3,197 lines at FIX ROUND 4 `22de1182`, already current with main) under the owner's PR size rule: over 3,000 changed lines is an automatic fail (MODEL_ROUTING.md 8.2, tgp-agent-context). Stack: P1 -> P2; merge back to back, deploy after P2. Migration 20270307000000 was edited in place during #648's fix rounds; confirm it is absent from production `_prisma_migrations` before deploy (read-only check). Tree at P2 = #648 head. Prior verdicts (Sol RC 0/1/0 at ab607b34) do not carry; each piece needs Opus 5.5 and Sol audits at its exact head. `tsc --noEmit` passes at both pieces; every existing spec importing a changed file was run locally.\n\n**P2 (base P1, 2,876 lines at 53796f1e):** push delivery service, notifications service and emitter wiring; delivery, send-time, emitter and booking-emitter specs. Locally 35 suites pass (528 tests; 4 live suites skipped without a database).\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-03T20:41:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T18:40:46Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ca95f8b4003c42b8975c7616f3859205cd6f4865","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":11278565662,"node_id":"LA_kwDORnQJEs8AAAACoEFBHg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/labels/size/size/XL","name":"size/size/XL","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-p